spans.s:
baka, m. a kind of heron (Ardea nivea: 🞄regarded as a type of circumspection as well 🞄as roguery and hypocrisy);
 rogue, cheat;
 🞄hypocrite;
 N.: -kaccha, m. Heron-bank, N. 🞄of a locality;
 -mūrkha, m. fool of a heron.

baka-ripu, m. foe of Baka (a Rākṣasa 🞄conquered by him), ep. of Bhīmasena;
 🞄-vatī, f. N. of a river;
 -vṛtti, a. behaving 🞄like the heron, hypocritical;
 m. hypocrite;
 🞄-vrata, n. action of heron: -cara, a. acting 🞄like a heron, hypocritical;
 -vratika, a. 🞄hypocritical;
 -vratin, a. id.;
 -sahavāsin, 🞄m. fellow-lodger of the heron = lotus;
 -ari, 🞄m. foe of Baka (an Asura), ep. of Kṛṣṇa;
 🞄-ālīna, pp. lurking like a heron.

bakula, m. a tree (Mimusops Elengi: 🞄said to blossom on being sprinkled with wine 🞄from the mouth of young women);
 n. Bakula 🞄flower: -mālā, f. N.;
 -āvalikā, f. N..
